    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57">

                <pb facs="0057" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/6–546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >O’Sullivan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-05T17:00:00+07:00">June 5, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 6—7:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Ho Chi Minh probably will call at AmEmbassy shortly. He has constantly given
                    me impression he would pay great attention to any suggestions made by Dept.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Sullivan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
